{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And from your seed you shall not give to pass through to Molech, nor shall you profane the name of your Elohim.</b> For when you offer to Elohim, blessed be He, other living beings, but to Molech you offer your son, it will appear from this that Molech is of greater rank than He, heaven forfend." "<b>I am HaShem.</b> I have not changed the oath I swore to be your Elohim, when I said to Abraham: לִהְיוֹת לְךָ לֵאלֹהִים וּלְזַרְעֲךָ אַחֲרֶיךָ (Genesis 17:7). And since He spoke of the forbidden unions in order to render the seed fit, so that His great name would be worthy to rest upon it, He also spoke of Molech — whose worshippers thought to prepare, through its worship, the rest of the seed for success — and said that through its worship there would be profanation of HaShem, causing the withdrawal of His Shekhinah from the rest of the seed."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:46.363394955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}